auth {
  mode: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Brighte API

  1. `cp .env.example .env` in this folder (passwords of the seed accounts, gitignored).
  2. Select the **local** environment.
  3. Run **1 Auth / Login as admin**. It stores the access token in `{{token}}`, which every
     request inherits as `Authorization: Bearer`. Tokens last 15 minutes: run it again when
     requests start returning `UNAUTHENTICATED`.

  Public operations (`login`, `register`, `serviceTypes`) send no token.
  **4 Access checks** logs in as the USER account, so run **Login as admin** again afterwards.

  Check `errors[0].extensions.code`, not the HTTP status. Codes: see the API reference
  (`pnpm --filter @brighte/api docs:build`).

  Command line: `pnpm dlx @usebruno/cli run --env local -r` from this folder.
}
